<title>USA: Citizens Utilities to buy Broken Hill unit.</title>
<headline>Citizens Utilities to buy Broken Hill unit.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citizens Utilities Co said Thursday it has definitively agreed to buy all outstanding stock of a gas distribution company owned by Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd for about $100 million.</p>
<p>The deal is subject to Hawaii Public Utilities Commission and federal regulatory approvals but is expected to close in mid-1997, the company said.</p>
<p>Broken Hill ADRs gained one Thursday afternoon to 29-3/4. Citizens Utilities shares were unchanged at 11.</p>
</text>
